# ==============================================================================
# PulseFeed - Environment Configuration (.env.local)
# ==============================================================================
#
# All keys are purely optional. If no keys are provided, PulseFeed runs seamlessly
# in curated fallback mode with high-fidelity, deterministic datasets out-of-the-box.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit your real API keys or .env.local to version control.
# Note that these environment variables do NOT have NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefixes,
# ensuring they are never bundled into client JavaScript or exposed to browsers.
#
# 1. NewsAPI.org (Live News Headlines)
# Get a free API key at: https://newsapi.org/register
# When configured, PulseFeed fetches live top headlines filtered by user categories.
# When absent or rate-limited, PulseFeed automatically falls back to curated news.
NEWS_API_KEY=

# 2. The Movie Database (TMDB) API v3 (Live Recommendations)
# Get a free API key at: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
# When configured, PulseFeed queries live trending movies and series.
# When absent or rate-limited, PulseFeed automatically falls back to curated picks.
TMDB_API_KEY=

# 3. Social Media Stream (Intentionally Mocked)
# Social content is intentionally simulated with realistic threads, verified badges,
# and live reaction metrics. No external Twitter/X or Meta API keys are required.
